  <name>Bangla Voice Clock</name>
  <name xml:lang="bn">বাংলা ভয়েস ক্লক</name>
  <summary>Tells the time aloud in Bangla</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="bn">বাংলায় সময় বলে দেয়</summary>

  <developer id="io.github.saifulmd0">
    <name>Saiful Islam</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      A free talking clock that announces the time in natural Bangla, the way it is said in
      Bangladesh: “এখন সময় সকাল দশটা বেজে বিশ মিনিট”. It sits in the panel and speaks every
      15, 30 or 60 minutes.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The part of the day (ভোর, সকাল, দুপুর, বিকাল, সন্ধ্যা, রাত), the exact minute, or the traditional quarters (সোয়া, সাড়ে, পৌনে)</li>
      <li>Two voices: Areeba AI, with a Bangladeshi accent, and the voice of the original 1998 Bangla Voice Clock</li>
      <li>Quiet hours to the minute, an optional chime and notification</li>
      <li>A timer that says the time left every minute</li>
      <li>Plays through the speakers or headphones you choose</li>
      <li>A Bangla or English window, in light or dark</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Announcements work offline. The successor of the Bangla Voice Clock for Windows (1998–2002)
      by Q A M Khaled Ferdaus.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.saifulmd0.BanglaVoiceClock.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
